A **Google Calendar** is not a relational database, but its data can be understood using a few logical tables. The main entities are **Calendars**, **Events**, **Attendees**, and **Reminders**.

### 1. Calendar Table

| Calendar ID | Calendar Name | Owner | Time Zone    |
| ----------- | ------------- | ----- | ------------ |
| cal_001     | Work          | Alice | Asia/Kolkata |
| cal_002     | Personal      | Alice | Asia/Kolkata |

---

### 2. Events Table

| Event ID | Calendar ID | Title          | Start Time       | End Time         | Location       | Description           |
| -------- | ----------- | -------------- | ---------------- | ---------------- | -------------- | --------------------- |
| evt_101  | cal_001     | Team Meeting   | 2026-07-03 10:00 | 2026-07-03 11:00 | Meeting Room A | Weekly sprint meeting |
| evt_102  | cal_001     | Client Demo    | 2026-07-04 15:00 | 2026-07-04 16:00 | Zoom           | Product demonstration |
| evt_103  | cal_002     | Birthday Party | 2026-07-05 18:00 | 2026-07-05 21:00 | Home           | Family celebration    |

---

### 3. Attendees Table

| Attendee ID | Event ID | Name  | Email                                         | Response Status |
| ----------- | -------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------- | --------------- |
| att_001     | evt_101  | Bob   | [bob@example.com](mailto:bob@example.com)     | Accepted        |
| att_002     | evt_101  | Carol | [carol@example.com](mailto:carol@example.com) | Pending         |
| att_003     | evt_102  | David | [david@example.com](mailto:david@example.com) | Declined        |

---

### 4. Reminders Table

| Reminder ID | Event ID | Method       | Minutes Before |
| ----------- | -------- | ------------ | -------------- |
| rem_001     | evt_101  | Notification | 30             |
