## Entity Relationship (ER) Structure

```text
Calendar
---------
CalendarID (PK)
CalendarName
Owner
TimeZone
      |
      | 1
      |
      | N
Events
------
EventID (PK)
CalendarID (FK)
Title
StartTime
EndTime
Location
Description
      |
      | 1
      |------ N Attendees
      |
      |------ N Reminders
      |
      |------ 0..1 Recurrence
```

### Example Scenario

**Calendar:** Work

**Event:** Team Meeting

* Date: 3 July 2026
* Time: 10:00 AM – 11:00 AM
* Location: Meeting Room A
* Attendees:

  * Bob (Accepted)
  * Carol (Pending)
* Reminder:

  * Notification 30 minutes before
  * Email 1 hour before
* Recurrence:

  * Every week until 31 December 2026

This structure is similar to how calendar systems (including Google Calendar APIs) organize data, with one calendar containing many events, and each event optionally having multiple attendees, reminders, and recurrence rules.

